From d675d6f5fbb19781ae7bb563917b32682240be53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:39:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] RvDocument: disconnect only RV's own menu connections
 when purging menus

purgeMenus() called QMenu::disconnect() with no arguments on every menu.
That wildcard disconnect also removes whatever else is connected to the
menu (including its destroyed() signal), and Qt 6 warns for each such
menu: "QObject::disconnect: wildcard call disconnects from destroyed
signal of QMenu::unnamed" -- 222 lines on every menu rebuild (mode
toggles) and on close. The only connections RvDocument makes on these
menus are aboutToShow() -> this, so disconnect just those.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/lib/app/RvCommon/RvDocument.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/lib/app/RvCommon/RvDocument.cpp b/src/lib/app/RvCommon/RvDocument.cpp
index 183e803..1da133c 100644
--- a/src/lib/app/RvCommon/RvDocument.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/app/RvCommon/RvDocument.cpp
@@ -2489,7 +2489,10 @@ namespace Rv
             if (QMenu* m = a->menu())
             {
                 disconnectActions(m->actions());
-                m->disconnect();
+                //  Only this document's connections (aboutToShow): a wildcard
+                //  disconnect() also cuts whatever else watches the menu's
+                //  destroyed() signal, and Qt 6 warns about each such menu.
+                m->disconnect(this);
             }
             else
                 a->disconnect();
